From 0a29b65b05818f5d05d0d0be480cc6499e1e4d16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:45:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): re-parks after a live probe fired never
 escalate; supervisor must be runnable

t_f6d930b7 (Upkeep P5 Mac) parks on a read-only probe, mac-final-ready.py, that exits 0 only while
the Mac is unlocked and HID idle > 900 s. The probe fired, but the user was back by the time a
worker ran, so the card re-parked on the same probe. prior_same_premise counted those re-parks as
one premise (same probe hash), and the third escalated: the card went to todo behind an
"Unstick ... parked 3x" owner and lost its wake_check. Both owners then went to mac-ops, which no
pool worker can run, so an orchestrator completed them by hand (11-11 22:30Z, 11-12 05:10Z).

- prior_same_premise: a condition_met wake by the same probe ends the trailing run. Its condition
  really held (two confirming exit-0 runs), so the next park waits on a natural window that closed
  again. That is new evidence, not a stuck premise. Parks woken only by their deadline, or after
  a different probe fired, still count and still escalate.
- _supervisor skips any candidate profile that a new scratch card could not run. That is the case
  when the card would enroll in this gateway's worker pool (portable, pool configured) and no
  active, unheld, picking-up pool member attests profile:<name>. An unreadable registry counts as
  none. Without a pool, or for a non-portable assignee, local profiles stay valid. With no runnable
  candidate the owner falls back to triage, as before.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_repark_natural_wait.py replays the t_f6d930b7 park shape
(awaiting clock 'Mac HID noninterference quiet window', wake_check set, check_every 300). On base,
5 of its 10 tests fail. All 10 pass with the fix, as do 1567 tests in the 59 files that touch the
awaiting, assignment-routing, no-progress, timed-park, schedule and wake-check paths.
